<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Achaea</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Achaea is a region in the northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnese">Peloponnese</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>, along the southern shore of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-of-corinth">Gulf of Corinth</a>, with its chief city at Patras. In antiquity it held twelve small cities whose federation, the Achaean League, became a leading power in Greece in the 3rd century BCE. After 1205 it was the heart of the Frankish Principality of Achaea.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/achaea.jpg" alt="Achaea" width="320" height="221" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Achaia_municipalities_numbered.svg: Badseed derivative work: Pitichinaccio (talk) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2010_Dimi_Achaias_numbered.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
